      "text": [
        ": تَذَاكَرُوا اَلشُّؤْمَ عِنْدَهُ فَقَالَ \"اَلشُّؤْمُ فِي ثَلاَثَةٍ فِي اَلْمَرْأَةِ وَ اَلدَّابَّةِ وَ اَلدَّارِ فَأَمَّا شُؤْمُ اَلْمَرْأَةِ فَكَثْرَةُ مَهْرِهَا وَ عُقُوقُ زَوْجِهَا وَ أَمَّا اَلدَّابَّةُ فَسُوءُ خُلُقِهَا وَ مَنْعُهَا ظَهْرَهَا وَ أَمَّا اَلدَّارُ فَضِيقُ سَاحَتِهَا وَ شَرُّ جِيرَانِهَا وَ كَثْرَةُ عُيُوبِهَا\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4912 - It is narrated from Khalid ibn Najeeh that Imam Abu Abdullah Al-Sadiq (as) said: They were discussing misfortune in his presence.\nImam (as) said: \"Misfortune lies in three things: in a woman, in a mount, and in a house.\nAs for the misfortune of a woman, it is in her high dowry and her disobedience to her husband.\nAs for the mount, it is in its bad temperament and its refusal to allow itself to be ridden.\nAnd as for the house, it is in its narrow space, its bad neighbors, and its many defects.\""
        ]
      }
    },
